BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260508T013000Z
DTEND:20260508T023000Z
UID:7cvfu7mkvpdelqfojfosaisg68@google.com
X-GOOGLE-CONFERENCE:https://meet.google.com/bkz-twfw-fam
CREATED:20260421T034635Z
DESCRIPTION:Directions: <a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/6NLiFodDU7kSeq1S7"
 >https://maps.app.goo.gl/6NLiFodDU7kSeq1S7</a><br><br><a href="https://www.
 lesswrong.com/users/vivek-1" target="_blank">https://www.lesswrong.com/user
 s/vivek-1</a><br><br>Vivek Hebbar is a Member of Technical Staff at Redwood
  Research\, where he works on AI control. He attended Stanford before joini
 ng MATS in 2022\, and has MATS Program since focused on control\, model org
 anisms\, scheming and deception\, and strategy and forecasting. <br><br>His
  published work engages with core problems in AI safety — including how mis
 aligned AI systems might engage in research sabotage by withholding ideas o
 r introducing subtle bugs\, and how AI control techniques might address suc
 h diffuse\, multi-action threats — as well as how capable agents with highe
 r-level goals might exploit learned heuristics to game training while outpe
 rforming reward-proximate models. He is also a mentor for the MATS Summer 2
 026 program.\n\nJoin with Google Meet: https://meet.google.com/bkz-twfw-fam
 \n\nLearn more about Meet at: https://support.google.com/a/users/answer/928
 2720
LAST-MODIFIED:20260507T235222Z
LOCATION:Humanities Interim Classroom Facility 100K
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Vivek Hebbar (Redwood Research) talk 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
